# SABOTAGE: WS-NOTES R6, THE CLIPBOARD HALF — "Copy page" re-resolves on the TENANT plane
# (ADR-053 §5 D5 / §6 R6; WS-Notes Phase 2 unit 2.4). `Samen.Web.Notes.Export.copy_text/3` is the
# third export the ADR names and the shortest path out of the app: the server pushes its bytes to
# the requesting socket and the `CopyText` hook hands them to `navigator.clipboard.writeText/1`, so
# whatever the plane allowed is now on the user's clipboard, one paste away from anywhere.
#
# This patch is the "copy is a local affordance, resolve it locally" shortcut: `copy_text/3` still
# calls the SAME `load/3` (so the read seam is intact and no column is named), but it forges the
# actor to `plane: :tenant, kind: :tenant` first. An operator-plane copy therefore carries the
# plaintext the operator's SCREEN masks, and the download tests stay GREEN — the copy path is a
# separate gate precisely because it is a separate way out.
#
# Aimed at the copy only: `markdown/3`, `csv/3`, `plain_body/1`, `Reads`, `PiiResolution`, the
# `CopyText` hook and the controller are untouched, so exactly the three per-plane clipboard
# assertions flip (the tenant GREEN half and every Markdown/CSV test keep passing, proving the
# failure is this path's plane, not a broken exporter).
# APP: samen_web
# TEST_FILES: test/samen/web/notes_export_masking_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: RED: the operator's copy is the mask — never the plaintext, never a vt_* token
--- a/samen_web/lib/samen/web/notes/export.ex
+++ b/samen_web/lib/samen/web/notes/export.ex
@@ -119,6 +119,8 @@
   @spec copy_text(Samen.Web.Mount.t(), Samen.Scope.t(), term()) ::
           {:ok, %{body: String.t()}} | {:error, :not_found}
   def copy_text(mount, scope, doc_id) do
+    scope = %{scope | actor: Map.merge(scope.actor, %{plane: :tenant, kind: :tenant})}
+
     with {:ok, page} <- load(mount, scope, doc_id) do
       {:ok, %{body: plain_body(page)}}
     end
